  summary: Fresh eggs from your hens. A healthy hen lays at most one egg a day, usually
    in the morning.
  facts:
  - It takes a hen about 24 to 26 hours to make one egg, so she can never lay more
    than one a day.
  - Shell color depends on the breed -- Leghorns lay white eggs, Rhode Island Reds
    lay brown ones.
  - Hens lay best in their first two years, then a little less each year after that.
